# Office lock/temp files
~$*.xlsx
~$*.xlsm
~$*.xlsb
~$*.docx
~$*.pptx
*.tmp
.~lock*

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Transient Power Automate test-run captures - for validating connector behavior in
# the moment, not a record worth keeping once the finding's written into the docs
workflow-data/*raw output*.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# handbook build output: regenerate with gen_handbook_docs.py + Convert-HandbookDocs.ps1
dist/

# Local backups taken before in-place workbook surgery (apply_bo_report_formatting.py).
# Kept on disk, deliberately out of git: an LFS copy of a one-off pre-change snapshot is
# not worth the storage. NOTE this means the .bak is the ONLY pre-change copy when the
# workbook itself was untracked before the surgery - as BO Report.xlsx was on 2026-09-11.
# Don't delete one until the changed workbook has been committed and eyeballed.
# *.bak, not *.xlsx.bak: the narrower pattern missed
# 'BO Report.xlsx.printsetup.bak' and a 105KB binary went into a commit that had
# just declared it ignored. Match the suffix, not a guessed middle.
*.bak
